{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And YHWH</b> — The reason is that they have a great sound; therefore 'the earth quaked at the sound of the teru‘ah,' as it says, 'all the inhabitants of the earth quake.' And the one who explains the name [as literal] — [saying] 'He informed you of this before it came' — this is not the way of the language. Rather, the sense is as though HaShem shook the earth, in the manner of 'from Zion He roars and from Jerusalem He gives forth His voice,' and he is prophesying about the earthquake; therefore he says, 'He roars over His habitation.' And there is no wondering how His voice is like the sound of an earthquake, for His camp is very great, like 'and the uproar of nations.'" "<b>Who does His word</b> — like: 'for My mouth is the one who gathers.'"], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The quotation הודיעכם זה לפני בואו may allude to an unidentified commentator or exegetical tradition; translated literally without resolving the reference."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:33.923253822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}